DFT+U + noncollinear SOC, Fe2, multiple k points

Numerical configuration
-----------------------
The wavefunction cutoff remains 10 Ry. The explicit 160 Ry charge-density
cutoff improves resolution of the nonlinear core correction compared with
the former implicit 40 Ry grid. This changes the numerical discretization
and its reference energy; it is not a claim of complete cutoff convergence.

The SCF threshold is 1e-11. pw_diag_thr sets the initial inner threshold;
pw_diag_thr_max=1e-14 also bounds later SCF diagonalizations. Empty-band
threshold smoothing is disabled. The larger iteration budgets allow these
accuracy checks without changing the harness acceptance tolerances.

Reference validation (2026-10-25)
-------------------------------
The reference is a fresh Davidson-subspace result, checked independently
with PPCG and Davidson after the rank-deficient-direction and PPCG direction
rotation fixes. GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, Release CPU; four MPI ranks;
OMP_NUM_THREADS=OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=MKL_NUM_THREADS=1.
All four solvers, including the supplementary CG run, reached SCF convergence
in 20 iterations. Absolute differences relative to PPCG were:

solver                 energy/eV       force sum/(eV/Angstrom)  stress sum/kbar
Davidson-subspace      2.20e-9         0 (printed precision)    1.00e-4
Davidson               1.16e-9         0 (printed precision)    9.20e-5
CG                     2.13e-9         2.00e-6                  2.218e-3
harness limit          1.00e-7         1.00e-4                  1.00e-3

Force and stress are the sums extracted by the original property collector.
The CG stress comparison remains outside the original limit. PPCG emitted
six early-iteration residual warnings at 1.07e-14 to 1.52e-14 against the
requested 1e-14; these warnings are retained. The final SCF and property
checks are reported separately. Repeating Davidson-subspace/PPCG with two
OpenMP threads also passed the same property limits.

Using 1e-13 inner thresholds removed the PPCG residual warnings, but degraded
the CG energy/force/stress agreement. That alternative was not adopted.
Neither the original failed runs nor their references were used as the new
cross-solver reference. The original files remain recoverable from Git.

Reproduce the native reference check from tests/01_PW:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \
    bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh -a /absolute/path/to/abacus -n4 -o1 -j1 \
    -r '^100_PW_DJ_SO$'

For a cross-solver check, copy the case and change only ks_solver to ppcg
or dav. Keep the reference and the harness tolerances unchanged. The timing
field is informational; these runs were not a controlled speed benchmark.
